## Back & Restart Buttons

### Back

- Dedicated nav row (left); move turn text to scoreboard
- Icon + `t(lang, 'back')` label (icon-only fallback on narrow screens)
- Ghost/outline on dark green — match Settings header pattern
- Reuse same component in `SettingsScreen.tsx` and both game views

### Restart

- Nav row (right); icon ↻ + optional short label
- **Confirmation dialog** before reset (prevents accidental taps)
- Destructive red only in confirm action, not as always-visible loud pill
- Win banner “Play Again” can call same `restart` after confirm or skip confirm on win state

---

## Scoreboard & Controls

### Scoreboard

- Labels 11–12px min; scores 18–22px
- Active player: filled accent or left accent bar (not border-only)
- Center stats: single line with dividers (`Cushions 2/3 · Balls 1/2`)
- Reduce emoji reliance — colored dot or marble indicator for P1/P2/AI
- Fix hardcoded `'⚪ Player 2'` in `FourBallView.tsx` — use i18n

### Technique row

- Segmented control (rounded track, sliding active indicator) for spin and english
- Section labels: “Spin” / “English” (10px uppercase muted)
- Power meter inside dark rounded card; cancel button aligned
- AI thinking: subtle animation instead of static gray text
- Revisit fixed 58px height — may need 64–72px; update `BOARD_UI_GAP` if changed

### Win state

- Overlay modal on dimmed table (trophy + winner + Play Again + Back to menu)
- Avoid inline gold banner that pushes layout

